<title>SINGAPORE: Inchcape first half net profit down 23 pct.</title>
<headline>Inchcape first half net profit down 23 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			 (in million S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	   23.80	  vs   30.87</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)  14.50	  vs   18.90</p>
<p>    Associates	    2.06	  vs   10.08</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)   10.00	  vs   10.00</p>
<p>    Turnover	    643.82	  vs  657.81</p>
<p>    Interest income     2.47	  vs    2.64</p>
<p>    Interest expense    4.40	  vs    2.99</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit     37.39	  vs   49.14</p>
<p>    Tax		    11.44	  vs   16.09</p>
<p>    Minorities   (loss) 2.15	  vs    2.18 (loss)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries(gain)8.35	 vs    5.22 (loss)</p>
<p>    Profit attributable 32.15	 vs   25.65</p>
<p>to shareholders</p>
<p>Note - Trading group Inchcape said profit after tax declined because of cessation of contribution from Rolex Singapore Pte Ltd and increased interest expense. Extraordinary gains were mainly from sale of surplus residential property. It said excluding the discontinued Rolex business, the group will be able to maintain a similar level of profit as in 1995.</p>
</text>
